Ecological systems are built on complex networks of interactions between species, populations and communities. Network analysis provides powerful tools for investigating these relationships, understanding ecological structure and exploring how ecosystems respond to environmental change.

This practical course introduces network analysis using R, covering the construction, visualisation and interpretation of ecological networks, alongside methods for investigating their structural properties and dynamics.

Topics include:

