PR Stats is pleased to announce an upcoming live online course of particular interest to researchers working in ecology, conservation, environmental science and related fields.

Hierarchical Generalized Additive Models for Biological Sciences (HGAM01)

Dates: 8?11 February 2027
Duration: 22 hours (4 days)
Format: Live Online via Zoom
Instructor: Dr Gavin Simpson
Course Fee: ?400

Ecological datasets frequently contain complex nonlinear relationships, repeated measurements and hierarchical structures, such as observations collected across different sites, populations, species or environmental conditions.

Hierarchical Generalized Additive Models (HGAMs) provide a flexible framework for modelling these relationships, allowing researchers to estimate both shared ecological responses and group-specific nonlinear trends.

This practical course will demonstrate how to fit, evaluate and interpret HGAMs in R using the mgcv package, with applications to ecological and environmental datasets.

Topics covered include:

  *   Modelling nonlinear ecological relationships using GAMs.

  *   Shared and group-specific smooths across sites, species or populations.

  *   Factor?smooth interactions and hierarchical GAM structures.

  *   Random effects, smoothing penalties and partial pooling.

  *   Modelling variation in ecological responses between groups.

  *   Model selection, diagnostics, inference and uncertainty.

  *   Visualising and interpreting complex ecological relationships.

Who should attend?

The course is suitable for PhD students, postdoctoral researchers and professionals working in ecology, conservation biology, environmental science and related disciplines who need to analyse nonlinear relationships in grouped or hierarchical datasets.

Participants should have some experience with R and regression modelling. Previous familiarity with GAMs is strongly recommended.

Recordings and materials

All sessions will be recorded and made available to participants, allowing researchers in different time zones to follow the course. R scripts, datasets and supporting course materials will also be provided.

Full course details and registration:

https://prstats.org/course/hierarchical-generalized-additive-models-for-biological-sciences-hgam01/

